Description: dashenc: backport Plex's seek-resume + URL-manifest additions
 Plex's ffmpeg fork adds four DASH muxer extensions that scaleplex's
 worker currently emulates with ugly external scaffolding:

  -manifest_name <url>       Write the manifest to a URL via HTTP PUT
                             instead of a local file. Avoids a separate
                             "watch + POST to relay" loop on the worker.

  -skip_to_segment N         Start segment numbering at N (default 1).
                             Lets PMS resume a seek transcode at a
                             specific segment index without renaming
                             chunks server-side. Sets
                             os->segment_index = N, adjusts duration
                             math, passes "fragments" to the movenc, and
                             tags the first chunk +frag_discont.

  -break_non_keyframes 1|0   Allow segment breaks on non-keyframes
                             (default 0). Used by Plex for audio-only
                             outputs where the only "key" packets are
                             the audio frames themselves.

  -delete_removed 1|0        Whether to physically delete segment files
                             once they fall out of the manifest window
                             (default 1, matches upstream behaviour).
                             Plex sets this to 0 so PMS can serve
                             rewind/early-fetch requests from segments
                             that have already slid off the live window.

 Without these, scaleplex's worker has to:
   - strip every flag at rewrite time;
   - inject `-extra_window_size 999999` to approximate
     `-delete_removed false`;
   - run a chunk-renumber fsnotify watcher that hardlinks ffmpeg's
     1-indexed output to the N-indexed names PMS expects on seek;
   - run a manifest-publisher goroutine that watches the `dash` file
     and POSTs each update to the relay.

 All of the above goes away once this patch lands — except the
 manifest-publish path which switches from "agent POSTs to relay" to
 "ffmpeg PUTs to relay directly" via the existing HTTP protocol
 handler inside libavformat.

 Plex's own fork uses the same logic; this is a straight port to
 jellyfin-ffmpeg's 7.1.3 base (which already merged the upstream
 `(c->use_template && !c->use_timeline)` short-circuit Plex relied on
 — we preserve the natural form rather than re-introducing the `|| 1`).

Origin: backport, https://github.com/plexinc/plex-media-server-ffmpeg-gpl
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-11
